msgid "Learning about parameters - tutorial"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:20
msgid ""
"Parameters are configuration values that let nodes change behavior without "
"changing code. In this article, you will use Turtlesim and command-line "
"tools to inspect, set, save, and reload ROS parameters. After you follow "
"these steps, you will be able to configure node behavior at runtime and from "
"a YAML file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:28
msgid ""
"Parameters are configuration values stored by each node in the ROS graph. "
"This article walks you through using the ``ros2 param`` command-line tools "
"to inspect, change, save, and reload parameters. A hands-on exercise with "
"Turtlesim shows how parameters control node behaviour at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:32
msgid "**Area: Framework | Content-type: tutorial | Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:36
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:39
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:41
msgid ""
"Each node in the ROS graph stores its own set of configuration values, "
"called parameters. Use the ``ros2 param`` commands to get, set, save, and "
"reload parameter values at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:44
msgid ""
"For more information, see :doc:`About parameters <../../../About-"
"Parameters>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:47
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:49
msgid ""
"You will need the :doc:`turtlesim package <../../../../Get-Started/"
"Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:52
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:55
msgid "Do not forget to source ROS in every new terminal you open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:57
msgid ""
"For more information, see :doc:`Configuring environment <../../../../Get-"
"Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:60
msgid "1 Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:62
msgid ""
"Start up the two Turtlesim nodes, ``/turtlesim`` and ``/teleop_turtle``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:64
msgid "Open a new terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:66
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:70
msgid "Open another terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:72
msgid "$ ros2 run turtlesim turtle_teleop_key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:78
msgid "2 View the list of parameters for your nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:80
msgid ""
"To see the parameters belonging to your nodes, open a new terminal and run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:82
msgid "$ ros2 param list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:86
msgid "You should see output similar to:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:88
msgid ""
"/teleop_turtle:\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability\n"
"  scale_angular\n"
"  scale_linear\n"
"  use_sim_time\n"
"/turtlesim:\n"
"  background_b\n"
"  background_g\n"
"  background_r\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history\n"
"  qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability\n"
"  use_sim_time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:108
msgid ""
"The output groups the parameters under each node name, ``/teleop_turtle`` "
"and ``/turtlesim``. The namespace and name of a parameter are separated by "
"dots, as in ``parameter_events.publisher.depth``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:111
msgid "Before you continue, notice the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:113
msgid ""
"``use_sim_time``: Specifies whether the node uses simulated time or the "
"computer's clock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:114
msgid ""
"``background_r``, ``background_g``, and ``background_b``: Define the RGB "
"values for the background colour of the Turtlesim window"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:118
msgid "3 Identify the type and value of a parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:120
msgid ""
"To display the type and current value of a parameter, use the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:122
msgid "$ ros2 param get <node_name> <parameter_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:126
msgid ""
"You can also query a parameter across all nodes by omitting the node name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:128
msgid "$ ros2 param get <parameter_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:132
msgid ""
"To find out the current value of ``/turtlesim``'s parameter "
"``background_g``, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:134
msgid "$ ros2 param get /turtlesim background_g"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:138
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:176
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:245
msgid "The terminal returns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:140
msgid "Integer value is: 86"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:144
msgid "This tells you ``background_g`` holds an integer value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:146
msgid ""
"Running the same command on ``background_r`` and ``background_b`` should "
"return the values ``69`` and ``255``, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:148
msgid ""
"You can also omit the node name. As an example, you can try querying "
"``use_sim_time``, because every node has it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:151
msgid "$ ros2 param get use_sim_time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:155
msgid "The command displays the value for each node that has that parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:158
msgid ""
"Omitting the node name works only on Lyrical, Rolling, and later "
"distributions. On earlier distributions, ``ros2 param get`` requires both a "
"node name and a parameter name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:162
msgid "4 Change a parameter value at runtime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:164
msgid "To change a parameter's value at runtime, use the following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:166
msgid "$ ros2 param set <node_name> <parameter_name> <value>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:170
msgid "Change ``/turtlesim``'s background colour:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:172
msgid "$ ros2 param set /turtlesim background_r 150"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:178
msgid "Set parameter successful"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:182
msgid "The background of the Turtlesim window should change colour, like this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:186
msgid ""
"Setting parameters with the ``set`` command will only change them in your "
"current session, not permanently. However, you can save your settings and "
"reload them the next time you start a node. See :ref:`dumping parameters "
"<DumpNodeParameters>` and :ref:`loading a parameter file on node startup "
"<LoadParameterFileOnNodeStartup>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:193
msgid "5 Save the parameters of a node to a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:195
msgid ""
"You can save parameters of a node to a file. This comes in handy if you want "
"to reload the node with the same parameters in the future. Use the following "
"command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:199
msgid "$ ros2 param dump <node_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:203
msgid ""
"The command prints to the standard output (stdout) by default, but you can "
"also redirect the parameter values into a file to save them for later. To "
"save your current configuration of ``/turtlesim``'s parameters into the file "
"``turtlesim.yaml``, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:206
msgid "$ ros2 param dump /turtlesim > turtlesim.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:210
msgid "A new file is created in the current working directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:212
msgid "Open the file to view the following content:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:214
msgid ""
"/turtlesim:\n"
"  ros__parameters:\n"
"    background_b: 255\n"
"    background_g: 86\n"
"    background_r: 150\n"
"    qos_overrides:\n"
"      /parameter_events:\n"
"        publisher:\n"
"          depth: 1000\n"
"          durability: volatile\n"
"          history: keep_last\n"
"          reliability: reliable\n"
"    use_sim_time: false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:231
msgid "6 Load node parameters from a file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:233
msgid ""
"You can load parameters from a file to a currently running node using the "
"following command:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:235
msgid "$ ros2 param load <node_name> <parameter_file>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:239
msgid ""
"To load the ``turtlesim.yaml`` file generated with ``ros2 param dump`` into "
"``/turtlesim`` node's parameters, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:241
msgid "$ ros2 param load /turtlesim turtlesim.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:247
msgid ""
"Set parameter background_b successful\n"
"Set parameter background_g successful\n"
"Set parameter background_r successful\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.depth' cannot be set "
"because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.durability' cannot be "
"set because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.history' cannot be set "
"because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability failed: "
"parameter 'qos_overrides./parameter_events.publisher.reliability' cannot be "
"set because it is read-only\n"
"Set parameter use_sim_time successful"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:260
msgid ""
"Read-only parameters can only be modified at startup and not afterwards, "
"which is why there are some ``failed`` warnings for the ``qos_overrides`` "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:265
msgid "7 Load parameter file on node startup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:267
msgid "To start the same node using your saved parameter values, use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:269
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run <package_name> <executable_name> --ros-args --params-file "
"<file_name>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:273
msgid ""
"This is the same command used to start Turtlesim, with the added flags ``--"
"ros-args`` and ``--params-file``, followed by the file you want to load."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:275
msgid ""
"Stop your running Turtlesim node, and try reloading it with your saved "
"parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:277
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run turtlesim turtlesim_node --ros-args --params-file turtlesim.yaml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:281
msgid ""
"The Turtlesim window should appear as usual, but with the purple background "
"you set earlier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters.rst:285
msgid ""
"When a parameter file is used at node startup, all parameters are updated, "
"including the read-only ones."
msgstr ""

